1
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:06,820
This is Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:31,540
You're on the move!

3
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,753
This place looks nothing like back home.

4
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:08,900
Of course not.

5
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:12,760
This is San Francisco, dude,
home of the Golden Gate Bridge.

6
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,477
Not to mention all the
seafood you can eat.

7
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:16,940
This isn't a vacation.

8
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:20,160
We're here to see Pegasus. She's right.

9
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:25,164
And based on the message he sent us, it
sounds like Pegasus is already in trouble.

10
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:29,580
This car, guarded with your
light, they mustn't find it.

11
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,876
Let's just hope we get to
him before those thieves do.

12
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:46,173
Seto, we're approaching Duelist Kingdom.

13
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,640
I'll try to make this quick.

14
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:52,240
The less time I spend
here, the better. Me too.

15
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,313
This place has nothing but bad memories.

16
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:59,100
Initiate the landing
sequence now. You got it.

17
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:03,722
We're beginning our descent
into Duelist Kingdom.

18
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:13,520
I'm sure his majesty is
somewhere in that castle.

19
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,920
Time to give him a royal beating.

20
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:33,940
Looks pretty empty in there I guess
Pegasus' staff is on vacation or something

21
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,397
That means less people to get on my nerves

22
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:40,260
Now let's find this
lunatic so we can leave

23
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:46,849
Airport staff is not responsible
for lost or damaged luggage

24
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,520
This was your dumbest idea yet, Weevil.

25
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:58,960
Who's Weevil?

26
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:08,720
You gotta love these steep roads.

27
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,740
Hey, check it out.

28
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,437
That's the Golden Gate Bridge, right?

29
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,680
The one and only.

30
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,640
It doesn't look gold to me.

31
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:17,697
You're taking all this in, Yugi?

32
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,220
Huh? What'd you say?

33
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:22,120
Hello, Earth to Yugi. Sorry, guys.

34
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:25,947
I can't stop thinking about
everything we found out this week.

35
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:29,137
It's not every day that
a magic gateway opens up

36
00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:31,977
between our world and a
world where monsters live.

37
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:33,178
And on top of that,

38
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:36,677
some kind of giant super monster
is trying to destroy both worlds.

39
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:39,877
And the only protection we
have against it is this card.

40
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,017
But even that doesn't seem to be enough.

41
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:45,335
Because that mega monster is
still out there somewhere.

42
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,800
I just don't know where.

43
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:51,771
We gotta get to the bottom of
this before it strikes again.

44
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,900
Maybe Pegasus just chickened out.

45
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,220
That is so not cool.

46
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,540
We could have fell down 200 feet.

47
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:09,000
I've just about run out of patience.

48
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:13,875
Show yourself, Pegasus, unless you've
come to your senses and gone home.

49
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:20,160
Your lack of patience
never fails to amuse me!

50
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:30,380
You're as irritating as ever!

51
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,916
Come on, where's the love, Kyber Boy?

52
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,760
After all, we've been through so much!

53
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:38,400
I didn't come here to catch up!

54
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:41,457
I came to duel you so
you'll get out of my life!

55
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:43,160
That's not nice.

56
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:45,980
What did I ever do to deserve such hatred?

57
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,860
It's a long list, and I'm short on time.

58
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,280
Most recently,

59
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,717
you stuck your nose where it didn't belong

60
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:55,577
when you started buying
up pieces of my company.

61
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:58,157
And I'm sure you're the
one who's been ruining my

62
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:01,097
reputation lately by
starting this monster scare,

63
00:05:01,180 --> 00:05:02,660
aren't you? Admit it!

64
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,857
You made it look like
Duel Monsters are taking

65
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:07,440
over the world just to get some attention!

66
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:10,197
Hmm, do you honestly believe that?

67
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:13,540
Or are you afraid to admit
what you truly think?

68
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:16,360
That maybe these duel monsters are real.

69
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,750
Ha!

70
00:05:17,833 --> 00:05:21,617
You should know by now that I don't
believe in your hocus-pocus magic tricks.

71
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:24,465
And I certainly don't
believe in real monsters.

72
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:28,497
You're still trying to get away with
that I don't believe in magic speech?

73
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:31,992
Don't you think it's time to
give that one a rest already?

74
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:36,980
Especially after the time we shared
not so long ago in this very castle.

75
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:43,840
His soul is mine But don't
worry, he won't be alone for long

76
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:45,790
No,

77
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:50,080
beat me in a duel and I'll
release him as promised But fail,

78
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:56,560
and not only will his soul remain in bondage
But yours will join it And of course,

79
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:57,530
as always,

80
00:05:57,613 --> 00:06:01,100
I stayed true to my promise
But you already know that

81
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,120
Not only did you lose our duel,

82
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:09,757
Kyber boy you've lost the only chance
you had at rescuing your baby brother.

83
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:11,020
You let him down.

84
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:13,182
But don't worry, my dear friend.

85
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:17,582
I'll spare you the agony of carrying
on in this world without him.

86
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:21,140
Meet the final fate of
your soul, Seto Kaiba!

87
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:27,160
That's enough! What's wrong?

88
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:31,597
Did it suddenly become a crime to reminisce
about old times with good friends,

89
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,820
Kaiba boy? Listen,

90
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:37,137
if you're trying to mess with my head by
bringing up what happened in the past,

91
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:38,617
I'm afraid it won't work.

92
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:39,760
That's old news.

93
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,337
This time, it's you who's gonna suffer.

94
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,596
Then let's get this duel on the road.

95
00:06:44,860 --> 00:06:47,640
It's time for the rematch of the century.

96
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:52,644
I think you'll find that this
arena looks frighteningly familiar.

97
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:04,820
Well, well, well, here we are again.

98
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:08,960
In the exact same spot where
I devastated you last time.

99
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:12,060
So, ready for a repeat performance?

100
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:15,920
Who knew I'd get to destroy
you twice in one lifetime?

101
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:19,560
Let's get this duel over with.

102
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:21,760
The sooner I annihilate you,

103
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:25,312
the sooner I can get out of
here and move on with my life.

104
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:29,060
Yeah, my brother's gonna
take you apart, Pegasus.

105
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:34,220
Mokuba, I see that you're still
Kaiba Boy's one and only fan.

106
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:37,280
Mokuba, just stay back. What?

107
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,148
What are you talking about?

108
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:42,380
Look, we both know what
this madman is capable of,

109
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,480
and I want you at a safe distance.

110
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,130
Fine.

111
00:07:46,213 --> 00:07:47,043
I'll stay.

112
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:50,860
The ultimate rematch is about to start.

113
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,375
We're making history.

114
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:55,900
The only thing that's
gonna be history is you.

115
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:02,942
I guess I'll be safe up here if
Pegasus decides to pull something.

116
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:05,099
I just hope my brother's all right.

117
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,370
Seto!

118
00:08:07,453 --> 00:08:09,314
Time to beat this jerk in his own game!

119
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:11,710
Let's start.

120
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:15,160
You've wasted enough of
my time already, Pegasus.

121
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:17,920
Is it me or are you always in a bad mood?

122
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:20,337
We're about to play a friendly game here,

123
00:08:20,420 --> 00:08:23,479
so why don't you do yourself
a favor and lighten up?

124
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:24,490
I will.

125
00:08:24,573 --> 00:08:26,320
Just as soon as I tear you apart.

126
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,060
Here we go.

127
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,300
Light's Duel!

128
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:41,240
Now, since we're playing on my
field today, I get to go first.

129
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,630
Better up.

130
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:46,660
I'll start by summoning Toon
Alligator in defense mode.

131
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:49,380
I know this strategy.

132
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,520
Next, I'll place one card face down.

133
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:55,540
Step up to the plate, Kaiba boy.

134
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:57,231
I know what you're up to.

135
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:58,400
Oh, really?

136
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:00,001
And what's that?

137
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:04,847
You're using the same monsters you used
in our first duel to mess with my head.

138
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:06,560
No. Who, me?

139
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:10,320
Honestly, you're thinking
about this way too much.

140
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,300
Is that so?

141
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,511
Well, here comes a little
something for you to think about.

142
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:21,500
Spear Dragon, attack his Toon
Alligator with Cyclone Blast!

143
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:27,657
Your pathetic little Toon is gone.

144
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:32,140
But since it was in defense mode, your
life points are safe, right? Wrong.

145
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:36,980
Thanks to my dragon's special
ability, you lose 300 of them.

146
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:41,460
Then Spear Dragon automatically
switches to defense mode.

147
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,360
Finally, I place two cards face down.

148
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,300
That ends round one.

149
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,620
Way to go, Seto!

150
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,440
I can't be on my legs!

151
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:58,980
Those are my legs!

152
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:04,400
Look, we just dropped in.

153
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,424
Hey, we don't want any trouble!

154
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:10,975
You twib should have thought about
that before you landed on our street.

155
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,120
Any ideas?

156
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:14,480
Here's one.

157
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:15,950
Help!

158
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:20,910
Excellent.

159
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,394
This card should spice things up a bit.

160
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:27,197
it's a magical little
number i like to call

161
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:30,497
toon table of contents
what on earth is that

162
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:33,657
it's a magic card that
allows me to draw any

163
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:36,357
card from my deck with
the word tune in the title

164
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:41,217
not again toon world don't
sound so disappointed

165
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:44,497
of all the cards i've created this one's

166
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:47,957
by far my favorite i'm
sure once you see it

167
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:52,160
you'll change your tune
presenting toon world

168
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:57,845
This magic card allows me to summon any
and all of my Toon Monsters to the field.

169
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:02,960
And Toon World's cost of admission
is a mere 1,000 life points!

170
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:11,876
Now why don't we start this show with
a new favorite of mine, shall we?

171
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:14,100
Toon Match Sorcerer!

172
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:18,120
He may seem harmless, but
he has quite the temper!

173
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,840
You're in my world now, Kaiba Boy!

174
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:26,808
Now that Pegasus played
his Toon World card,

175
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,117
he can summon any Toon Monster he wants.

176
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,729
And he's got tons of them!

177
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:35,668
It's time to give you a taste
of your own medicine with this!

178
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:38,160
My cloning trap card!

179
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,904
Why don't you try dueling
with some originality?

180
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:44,820
What's the problem, Pegasus?

181
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:48,637
Are you annoyed because I've made
it pointless for you to attack?

182
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,880
What do you mean?

183
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:55,540
I mean that one of us was using his brain
today, and I'm not talking about you.

184
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:59,746
Now, if you attack me, you'll
destroy your own monster as well.

185
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:01,373
Care to give it a shot?

186
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,480
You've saved yourself for now. No kidding.

187
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:08,380
Next, I'll play my favorite card. Ready?

188
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:12,337
I sacrifice Spear Dragon
and Tomb Mask Sorcerer.

189
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:13,780
Oh, no!

190
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,740
Is that what I think it is?

191
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:20,000
I summon my blue-eyes white dragon!

192
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,845
That's what I'm talking about!

193
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,680
He's hungry, and your toon is on the menu.

194
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:35,177
He'll have to starve, because
in case you've forgotten,

195
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:38,077
my toons can only be
destroyed by other toons.

196
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:42,580
I'm well aware of that, but I
won't let a technicality stop me.

197
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:45,597
Well, then maybe I can
stop you with this trap.

198
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:46,510
What?

199
00:12:46,593 --> 00:12:48,980
I activate Tomb Mask.

200
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:58,600
This card lets me trade in my sorcerer
for a tomb version of your monster.

201
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,150
A what?

202
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:03,540
Say hello to my blue-eyes tomb dragon.

203
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:11,757
You know how much I hate that thing
Your cartoon dragon is a disgrace

204
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:16,160
to the original blue eyes Don't you
realize cartoons have feelings too?

205
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:23,600
Well, let's see how he feels about my next
card I activate the magic card, Shrink

206
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:28,860
It makes your puny dragon even punier

207
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,320
So what?

208
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,969
He's still indestructible.

209
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:37,060
All you did was make my
monster more lovable.

210
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:40,972
I'm through dealing with your
pitiful excuse for a dragon,

211
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:43,296
so let's focus on the real Blue Eyes.

212
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:48,440
This card makes its
attack even more fierce.

213
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:52,160
It isn't going to work.

214
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:56,307
Which part of Toons can't be
destroyed, didn't you understand?

215
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:59,320
Blue Eyes, attack with White Lightning!

216
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:09,040
Are we clear now on the whole
toons being indestructible thing?

217
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:14,200
Yes, but you seem to have forgotten
about my Charm of Lamentation Magic card!

218
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,400
What about it?

219
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:17,680
As long as it remains on the field,

220
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:20,637
I get to draw one card
from my deck every time

221
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:23,377
my Blue Eyes White
Dragon attacks and fails!

222
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:27,520
And since your toons can't be
destroyed, I'll keep drawing cards.

223
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:31,821
The key to beating this washed-up
has-been is somewhere in my deck.

224
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,982
I just have to keep picking
cards till I find it.

225
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,280
Back to me.

226
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:40,320
I'll start by giving up
500 of my life points.

227
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:44,920
This allows my blue-eyes toon dragon
to attack your life points directly.

228
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:49,760
The time has come, my angry little toon.

229
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:52,720
Unleash your fury upon Kaiba, boys.

230
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:55,000
I don't think so.

231
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:56,720
Negate attack!

232
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,400
You're no fun.

233
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:02,617
This trap card
automatically puts an end to

234
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:05,465
your attack before it's
able to hit its target.

235
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:08,760
So you spent your life points for nothing.

236
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,920
I have to disagree.

237
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:13,960
Thanks to a magic card
called Toon Rollback.

238
00:15:17,420 --> 00:15:21,740
This lets me rewind our duel,
giving me a second chance to attack.

239
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,310
Hold on.

240
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:25,997
The rollback card doesn't
work that way, Pegasus.

241
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:29,860
Your blue-eyes tomb dragon still
can't attack twice in one turn.

242
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:32,800
That's not my plan. Shame on you.

243
00:15:33,780 --> 00:15:38,520
I'd suggest paying attention instead
of jumping to conclusions. Just go.

244
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:43,400
As I was saying, I have no intention
of attacking you with my dragon again.

245
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,270
No.

246
00:15:45,353 --> 00:15:47,540
He's no longer of any use to me.

247
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:50,960
So I've decided to trade
him in for something better.

248
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,520
Oh, Doondock Magician Girl!

249
00:16:02,140 --> 00:16:04,900
Attack Kaiba Boy's lifeboards, won't you?

250
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:15,720
She packs quite a little
punch, doesn't she?

251
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,317
And so do I!

252
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,420
Watch this!

253
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:23,460
Blue-Eyes attack his
Toon Dark Magician Girl!

254
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:32,140
But those Toon monsters can't
be destroyed by Blue-Eyes! Seto!

255
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:39,600
Ta-da!

256
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:49,800
Remember, every time my
blue-eyes attack fails, I draw.

257
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:54,760
I must have missed the joke.

258
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:57,580
You are a joke, Pegasus.

259
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:01,460
You're just as outdated
as your strategies.

260
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:05,897
Your toon monsters may be indestructible,

261
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:10,039
But only as long as you have your
Toon World magic card on the field.

262
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,927
Without it, they're history.

263
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,260
So, what's your point?

264
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:18,260
I activate the magic card,
a wingbeat of giant dragon!

265
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,880
What do you plan to do with that?

266
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:25,840
First, I'll return my
blue eyes to my hand.

267
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:31,000
Then I can wipe all magic and trap
cards from your side of the field.

268
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:34,480
Which means your Toon World is toast!

269
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:49,440
Oh, my precious Toon World!

270
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,740
Nice one, Seto! You did it!

271
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:55,220
I never doubted you for a second!

272
00:17:56,420 --> 00:18:00,160
I'll finish by summoning Versago
the Destroyer in defense mode!

273
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,720
Your move, Pegasus!

274
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:04,630
Hello!

275
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:09,300
Last chance, then I win.

276
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:14,180
I'm taking your silence as a
forfeit, not that I blame you.

277
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:17,262
I'd quit too if my strategy
was as lame as yours.

278
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:23,000
You're using the exact same tactics
you used the first time we dueled here.

279
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,900
In fact, you've almost made
the same moves card for card.

280
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:28,820
What's the deal, Pegasus?

281
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:32,640
You're a lot of things, but
predictable isn't one of them.

282
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,200
I just haven't been myself lately.

283
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:37,337
In fact...

284
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:39,067
I mean that quite literally.

285
00:18:39,860 --> 00:18:42,240
What's going on? Surprise!

286
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:52,120
I've waited for this day
for a long time, Kaiba boy.

287
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:54,617
You're gonna pay for
tricking me like that.

288
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:56,420
Pretty good imitation, right?

289
00:18:57,240 --> 00:18:58,500
Identify yourself.

290
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,700
Alistair's the name Kaiba boy.

291
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,160
Now let's duel!

292
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:09,600
This magic card is about
to change everything.

293
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:12,340
Activating Seal of Orychalcos.

294
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,800
What's that?

295
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,180
This is nuts!

296
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,120
Explain yourself now!

297
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:33,000
Oh, as if you're gonna believe me? Try me.

298
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,357
We're trapped in here
till the duel's over.

299
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:38,860
Then, once I crush you,
I'll be able to get out.

300
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:44,346
Of course, you, on the other hand, won't
be quite as lucky as myself, Kaiba boy.

301
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:45,560
What do you mean?

302
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:51,000
When you lose, your soul will
be locked away for all eternity.

303
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:54,577
But this time, you won't be set free.

304
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:57,177
We'll

305
00:19:57,260 --> 00:20:03,020
be right back.

306
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:25,490
Thank you.
